<p>North Korea’s ruling Workers’ Party re-elected Kim Jong Un as general secretary at a party congress, keeping him in the country’s top political post. State media said the country’s nuclear-centered “war deterrence” had been significantly strengthened under his leadership. Kim said the party’s priorities are economic construction and raising living standards, even as official coverage emphasized defence capabilities.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MnupFTPsCPQsgjy8G9d9bp5j8kQfy8rtA6p-OkEISoShsAzUPBrJTK-OLhn5I3apr1ZoVefEKD2ja4rVAVZEQ66HjifL-bvcJclzcuEUKWDOviwty3QgQVqT7s6eXNEO_KVM5wDx9SVEqIeKWRzyxCuEWkhzEbwFRsFTnwOg1sJ9SlI7AI-sJfkolfd-HEyTZ2t07LucW9JdVmiHnkpAurPFD7E_1rT6bHesv7kKTBBD0XzH2rlEvC1U11hSNB_oydHAAg' alt='Kim Jong Un at the Workers’ Party congress where delegates re-elected him as general secretary.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Rare congress framing: Firstpost described the gathering as a rare party congress used to showcase nuclear advances and send a defiant message to global rivals.</li><li>Political weight: DW described the Workers’ Party congress as North Korea’s most important political event.</li><li>Significance of the post: France24 noted that the general secretary position is the most powerful role in the one-party state.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>North Korean state media (KCNA): KCNA cast the re-election as proof that Kim’s leadership has strengthened a nuclear-backed “war deterrence.” (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/north-koreas-kim-re-elected-to-lead-ruling-party-at-congress-report/article70664753.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Kim Jong Un: Kim said the party’s work is focused on “boosting economic construction and the people’s standard of living.” (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/north-koreas-kim-jong-un-re-elected-as-chief-of-workers'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>BBC analysis: The BBC described the congress as a managed “rubber-stamp” event and said the leadership announcement came as no surprise. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg18588mdko'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Delegates at the congress: Delegates credited Kim with bolstering North Korea’s nuclear arsenal and strengthening its regional standing, according to wire reporting. (<a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/kim-reelected-top-post-north-koreas-ruling-party-130396302'>ABC News</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/kim-reelected-top-post-north-koreas-ruling-party-130396302'>Kim reelected to top post of North Korea’s ruling party</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/shorts/watch-north-koreas-kim-jong-un-re-elected-as-party-general-secretary/article70665731.ece'>Watch: North Korea’s Kim Jong Un re-elected as party general secretary</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/kim-re-elected-as-north-korea-flaunts-nuclear-advances-at-rare-party-congress-13982670.html'>Kim re-elected as North Korea flaunts nuclear advances at rare party congress</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-ruling-party-reelects-kim-as-general-secretary/a-76081498'>North Korea: Ruling party reelects Kim as general secretary</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/2/22/north-koreas-kim-jong-un-re-elected-as-chief-of-workers'>North Korea’s Kim Jong Un re-elected as chief of Workers’ Party</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvg18588mdko'>Kim Jong Un re-appointed leader of North Korea&#x27;s ruling party</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20260222-north-korea-kim-re-elected-ruling-party-congress'>North Korea&#x27;s supreme leader, Kim Jong Un, is re-elected as the General Secretary of the Workers&#x27; Party of Korea, the most powerful position in the one-party state.</a> - france24.com</li></ul>